<title>USA: BankUnited gets merger approval.</title>
<headline>BankUnited gets merger approval.</headline>
<dateline>CORAL GABLES, Fla. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankUnited Financial Corp said it received approval from the U.S. Office of Thrift Supervision to acquire Suncoast Savings &amp; Loan Association of Hollywood, Fla.</p>
<p>BankUnited said the transaction is expected to close by mid-November, pending approval of Suncoast shareholders at a meeting scheduled for November 12.</p>
<p>The acquisition would boost BankUnited's assets to about $1.3 billion from $824 million at the end of the third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Under a merger agreement, Suncoast holders would get one BankUnited class A share for each Suncoast share.</p>
<p>BankUnited was up 1/8 at 9-1/8 at midday Thursday. Suncoast was unchanged at 8-1/2.</p>
